<h1>John Kelly</h1>
<p>Candidate for Mayor, Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027</p>
<p><a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website</a></p>
<p><a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com/issues/" rel="nofollow noopener">John Kelly&#39;s campaign lists five issues, each with a written explanation. Tap here to read them on his site, then come back to comment.</a></p>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>The platform</h3>
<p>Safety: Safe streets come first, through well-resourced police working with neighborhoods and violence prevention programs that have shown results.</p>
<p>Property taxes: Bring bills down by filling empty offices and attracting employers so more payers share the load, not by spending cuts alone.</p>
<p>Schools: Refocus CPS on reading, writing, and math. Kelly says Chicago Teachers Union leadership has drifted from the classroom and that teachers are not the problem.</p>
<p>City Hall: A CTA that is safe at every hour, and a city charter, a local constitution Chicago lacks, so ethics and spending rules can be enforced.</p>
<h3>Next to the other candidates</h3>
<p>Only Kelly: A city charter as a central plank, and the &quot;Safety Tax&quot;, what riders spend on ride-shares when the CTA feels unsafe at night.</p>
<p>Taxes: Mendoza, Kelly, and Brewer say relief comes from a bigger tax base. Holberg and Wilson promise lower taxes, and Carlisle proposes a new income tax tied to pension reform.</p>
<p>Transit: Mendoza and Cardenas would put police on the CTA, and Kelly wants it safe at every hour. Carlisle and Su would run trains and buses more often.</p>
<p>Not covered: Housing, which most other candidates address.</p>
